In 2014, state[ lawmakers] enacted a law permitting licensed inspectors to inspect home day[care centers] unannounced to ensure compliance with laws and regulations governing the operations of child[ care facilities].[ As] a result of the new law, which was enacted following the death of a 3-month-old infant in Greenville County, DSS inspectors have closed over 50 child dayc[ares] since 2014.
