> A free-standing, exterior, sculptural work for the Greenwood Neighborhood Fire Station[.] In moments of crisis and times of peace, fire stations[ are be]acons of safety embedded in our urban infrastructure[.] This sculpture is inspired by the multi-layered processes of fire fighting and aid response,[ with] attention to how crisis changes our relationship to space and[ time].[ Color] change triggered by station alarm system. Lead Artist. Photo Credit: Spike Mafford.


